   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |__________ WRITE PROT*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |______________ 0 RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |__________________ ONLINE*   |   |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|______________________ 0 RESERVED*   |______________________________________________________________ BLK FLAG******************************************************************		export	dstat_tbldstat_tbl		dc.w	dstat1		; pointer to status for DIB 1 device		dc.w	dstat2		; pointer to status for DIB 2 device		dc.w	dstat3		; pointer to status for DIB 3 device		dc.w	dstat4		; pointer to status for DIB 4 device		dc.w	dstat5		; pointer to status for DIB 5 device		dc.w	dstat6		; pointer to status for DIB 6 device		dc.w	dstat7		; pointer to status for DIB 7 device		dc.w	dstat8		; pointer to status for DIB 8 device		dc.w	dstat9		; pointer to status for DIB 9 device		dc.w	dstat1		; pointer to status for DIB A device		dc.w	dstatB		; pointer to status for DIB B device		dc.w	dstatC		; pointer to status for DIB C device		dc.w	dstatD		; pointer to status for DIB D device		dc.w	dstatE		; pointer to status for DIB E device		export	dstat1dstat1		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat2dstat2		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat3dstat3		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat4dstat4		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat5dstat5		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat6dstat6		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat7dstat7		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat8dstat8		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstat9dstat9		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstatAdstatA		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstatBdstatB		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstatCdstatC		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstatDdstatD		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		export	dstatEdstatE		dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block count		eject******************************************************************* The following flag is initially set to zero on loading of the* device driver.  If DISK][ hardware is found, a VBL task is* installed to simulate disk switched errors for the DISK][.* If this task is intalled, the VBL_TASK_FLAG will be nonzero.******************************************************************		export	vbl_task_flagvbl_task_flag		dc.w	0		; nonzero if task already installed		export	access_flagaccess_flag		dc.w	0		; 1=256 byte, 2=512 byte******************************************************************* The following flag is is used to generate a unique device* name for each DISK][ device during startup.******************************************************************		export	unique_nameunique_name		dc.b	'A '		; Always start with DISK][A******************************************************************* The following table is used by the VBL task to simulate* disk switched status for device access.******************************************************************		export	dsw_timersdsw_timers		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #1		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #2		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #3		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #4		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #5		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #6		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #7		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #8		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #9		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #A		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #B		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #C		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #D		dc.w	0		; timer for DIB device #E		eject******************************************************************* This data area is used to save absolute zero page locations* used on driver calls which are translated to the DISK][* core routines ported from the SOS driver.******************************************************************		export	azp_saveazp_save		DS.B	zp_size		eject******************************************************************* The following table is an image of the RWTS I/O Block* maintained in the current bank and used to translate calls* into bank $00 prior to calling RWTS.******************************************************************		export	my_iobmy_iob		export	my_ibtypemy_ibtype	dc.b	$01		; RWTS IOB Type		export	my_ibslotmy_ibslot	dc.b	$60		; slot * 16		export	my_ibdrvnmy_ibdrvn	dc.b	$01		; drive number  ($01 or $02)		export	my_ibvolmy_ibvol	dc.b	$00		; volume number ($00 = wildcard)		export	my_ibtrkmy_ibtrk	dc.b	$00		; track number  ($00 - $34)		export	my_ibsectmy_ibsect	dc.b	$00		; only used by format routine		export	my_ibwpbitmy_ibwpbit	dc.w	0		; word status from rwts =0000/0004=WP		export	my_ibbufpmy_ibbufp	dc.l	0		; I/O buffer pointer (in bank $00)		export	my_ibcmdmy_ibcmd	dc.b	$01		; RWTS command		export	my_ibstatmy_ibstat	dc.b	$00		; RWTS status		export	my_ibsmodmy_ibsmod	dc.b	$00		; volume number of disk found in drive		export	iobpsnxxiobpsnxx	dc.b	$00		; last slot number accessed		export	iobpdnxxiobpdnxx	dc.b	$00		; last drive number accessed** The followint is the device characteristics table for the Disk][*		export	d2_ibdctd2_ibdct	dc.b	$00		; Disk][		dc.b	$01		; Fixed parameter		dc.b	$EF,$D8		; Disk][ Motor on time		entry	format_volnumformat_volnum	dc.w	$00		; volume # to use when formatting		entry	rwts_volnumrwts_volnum	dc.w	$00		; volume # to pass to RWTS		eject******************************************************************* The following tables are used to select the interleave for* the Disk][.  Note that each block size may require a specific* interleave.******************************************************************		export	interleave_512interleave_512				dc.b	$0,$8,$1,$9,$2,$a,$3,$b,$4,$c,$5		dc.b	$d,$6,$e,$7,$f				export	interleave_256interleave_256		dc.b	0,$7,$e,$6,$d,$5,$c,$4,$b,$3		dc.b	$a,$2,$9,$1,$8,$f		eject******************************************************************* 7-bit to 6-bit 'deniblize' table (16-sector format)** Valid codes $96 to $FF only.** Codes with more than one pair of adjacent zeroes or with no* adjacent ones (except bit 7) are excluded.** nibls in the ranges of $a0-$a3, $c0-$c7, $e0-$e3 are used for* other tables since no valid nibls are in these ranges.******************************************************************		export	my_dniblmy_dnibl		dc.b	$00,$04		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$08,$0C		dc.b	$FF,$10,$14,$18		export	my_twobit3my_twobit3	dc.b	$00,$80,$40,$C0	; used in fast prenib as lookup for 2-bi		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$1C,$20		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$FF,$24		dc.b	$28,$2C,$30,$34		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$38,$3C		dc.b	$40,$44,$48,$4C		dc.b	$FF,$50,$54,$58		dc.b	$5C,$60,$64,$68		export	my_twobit2my_twobit2	dc.b	$00,$20,$10,$30	; used in fast prenib.		export	my_endmrksmy_endmrks	dc.b	$DE,$AA,$EB,$FF	; using 'unused' nibls ($c4 c5 c6 c7)		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$FF,$6C		dc.b	$FF,$70,$74,$78		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$FF,$7C		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$80,$84		dc.b	$FF,$88,$8C,$90		dc.b	$94,$98,$9C,$A0		export	my_twobit1my_twobit1	dc.b	$00,$08,$04,$0C	; used in fast prenib.		dc.b	$FF,$A4,$A8,$AC		dc.b	$FF,$B0,$B4,$B8		dc.b	$BC,$C0,$C4,$C8		dc.b	$FF,$FF,$CC,$D0		dc.b	$D4,$D8,$DC,$E0		dc.b	$FF,$E4,$E8,$EC		dc.b	$F0,$F4,$F8,$FC		eject******************************************************************* Page align the following tables.* 6-bit to 2-bit conversion tables.** dnibl2 abcdef-->0000fe* dnibl3 abcdef-->0000dc* dnibl4 abcdef-->0000ba******************************************************************** 6-bit to 7-bit nibl conversion table** Codes with more than one pair of adjacent zeroes or with no* adjacent ones (except b7) are excluded.******************************************************************		export	my_dnibl2my_dnibl2	dc.b	$00		export	my_dnibl3my_dnibl3	dc.b	$00		export	my_dnibl4my_dnibl4	dc.b	$00		export	my_niblmy_nibl		dc.b	$96,$02,$00,$00,$97		dc.b	$01,$00,$00,$9A,$03,$00,$00,$9B		dc.b	$00,$02,$00,$9D,$02,$02,$00,$9E		dc.b	$01,$02,$00,$9F,$03,$02,$00,$A6		dc.b	$00,$01,$00,$A7,$02,$01,$00,$AB		dc.b	$01,$01,$00,$AC,$03,$01,$00,$AD		dc.b	$00,$03,$00,$AE,$02,$03,$00,$AF		dc.b	$01,$03,$00,$B2,$03,$03,$00,$B3		dc.b	$00,$00,$02,$B4,$02,$00,$02,$B5		dc.b	$01,$00,$02,$B6,$03,$00,$02,$B7		dc.b	$00,$02,$02,$B9,$02,$02,$02,$BA		dc.b	$01,$02,$02,$BB,$03,$02,$02,$BC		dc.b	$00,$01,$02,$BD,$02,$01,$02,$BE		dc.b	$01,$01,$02,$BF,$03,$01,$02,$CB		dc.b	$00,$03,$02,$CD,$02,$03,$02,$CE		dc.b	$01,$03,$02,$CF,$03,$03,$02,$D3		dc.b	$00,$00,$01,$D6,$02,$00,$01,$D7		dc.b	$01,$00,$01,$D9,$03,$00,$01,$DA		dc.b	$00,$02,$01,$DB,$02,$02,$01,$DC		dc.b	$01,$02,$01,$DD,$03,$02,$01,$DE		dc.b	$00,$01,$01,$DF,$02,$01,$01,$E5		dc.b	$01,$01,$01,$E6,$03,$01,$01,$E7		dc.b	$00,$03,$01,$E9,$02,$03,$01,$EA		dc.b	$01,$03,$01,$EB,$03,$03,$01,$EC		dc.b	$00,$00,$03,$ED,$02,$00,$03,$EE		dc.b	$01,$00,$03,$EF,$03,$00,$03,$F2		dc.b	$00,$02,$03,$F3,$02,$02,$03,$F4		dc.b	$01,$02,$03,$F5,$03,$02,$03,$F6		dc.b	$00,$01,$03,$F7,$02,$01,$03,$F9		dc.b	$01,$01,$03,$FA,$03,$01,$03,$FB		dc.b	$00,$03,$03,$FC,$02,$03,$03,$FD		dc.b	$01,$03,$03,$FE,$03,$03,$03,$FF**  nibl buffer for read/write of low 2-bits of each byte.*		export	my_nbuf2my_nbuf2		dcb.b	86,0		eject******************************************************************* Phase on-, off-time tables in 100-usec intervals. (seek)******************************************************************		export	my_ontablemy_ontable	dc.b	$01,$30,$28,$24,$20,$1E,$1D,$1C,$1C		export	my_offtablemy_offtable	dc.b	$70,$2C,$26,$22,$1F,$1E,$1D,$1C,$1C		export	my_curtrkmy_curtrk	dc.b	$00		export	my_drv0trkmy_drv0trk	DS.B	16		; current track (slot/drive 10 - F0)		entry	my_retrycntmy_retrycnt	dc.b	0		entry	my_seekcntmy_seekcnt	dc.b	0		export	my_countmy_count		export	my_lastmy_last		dc.b	$00		export	my_csummy_csum		dc.b	$00		export	my_csstvmy_csstv	dc.b	$00		export	my_sectmy_sect		dc.b	$00		export	my_trackmy_track	dc.b	$00		export	my_volumemy_volume	dc.b	$00		export	my_priormy_prior	dc.b	$00		export	my_trknmy_trkn		dc.b	$00		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER MAIN ENTRY POINT: DISPATCH** This is the main entry point for the device driver.  The* routine validates the call number prior to dispatching to* the requested function.** Call Number: $0000    Function: Startup*              $0001              Open*              $0002              Read*              $0003              Write*              $0004              Close*              $0005              Status*              $0006              Control*              $0007              Flush*              $0008              Shutdown** ENTRY: Call via 'JSL'*     [<drvr_dib_ptr] = Points to the DIB for the device being accessed*       <drvr_dev_num = Device number of device being accessed*      <drvr_call_num = Call number*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT:   Direct page = unchanged with the exception of <drvr_tran_cnt*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************dispatch	PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on		phb			; save environment		phk		plb		cmp	#max_command	; is it a legal command?		bge	illegal_req	; no		tay			; save command #		ldx	#$0000save_parms		lda	<drvr_dev_num,x	; save GS/OS call parameters		pha		lda	<drvr_blk_num,x		pha		inx		inx		cpx	#$000C		; up to but not including DRVR_TRAN_CNT		bne	save_parms		tya			; restore command #		asl	a		; make index to dispatch table		tax		jsr	(|dispatch_table,x)		tay			; save error code		ldx	#$000A		; number of words to restorerestore_parms		pla			; restore GS/OS call parameters		sta	<drvr_blk_num,x		pla		sta	<drvr_dev_num,x		dex		dex		bpl	restore_parms		plb		bcs	gen_exit	; force error code 0 if flag cleared		ldy	#no_errorgen_exit		tya			; restore error code		rtl** Received an illegal request.  Return with an error.*illegal_req		plb			; restore environement		lda	#drvr_bad_req	; set error		sec		rtl		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  STARTUP** This routine must prepare the driver to accept all other driver* calls.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSR'*     [<drvr_dib_ptr] = Points to the DIB for the device being accessed*       <drvr_dev_num = Device number of device being accessed*      <drvr_call_num = Call number*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*         Direct page = unchanged with the exception of <drvr_tran_cnt*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************startup		PROC		Import	chkdrv0					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on		ldy	#slot_num	; slot to check for hardware		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y*** Added - 2-Apr-93 JCM - Store a clean copy of the slot number back into our***			   DIB. We'll update the internal/external bit after***			   we get done searching.		and	#$0007		;just keep slot number 0-7		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		*** End - 2-Apr-93 JCM		tay		xba		ora	#$C001		; create $Cn01		tax		sep	#$20		; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		lda	>0,x		; $Cn01 s/b $20		cmp	#$20		bne	@no_disk2		inx		inx		lda	>0,x		; $Cn03 s/b $00		bne	@no_disk2		inx		inx		lda	>0,x		; $Cn05 s/b $03		cmp	#$03		bne	@no_disk2		lda	#$FF		tax		lda	>0,x		; $CnFF s/b $00		beq	@found_hardware@no_disk2		brl	no_disk2@found_hardware;;; Removed 12-Aug-92 DAL;*;* Disk][ hardware was located.  Make sure there's actually;* a drive connected.;*;		phy			; save slot #;		phb			; save my DBR;		pea	$0000		; set to bank 0;		plb;		plb;;		sep	#$30		; 8-bit registers;		longa	off;		longi	off;		;		tya			; get $x0 into X;		asl	a;		asl	a;		asl	a;		asl	a;		tax;;		ldy	#unit_num	; get drive #;		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y;		lsr	a		; drive 1 or 2?;		bcc	@drive_2	; drive 2...;		lda	|drv0en,x	; enable drive 1;		bra	@1;@drive_2;		lda	|drv1en,x	; enable drive 2;@1;		lda	|motoron,x	; turn on the drive motor;;		lda	|cyareg		; save current setting;		pha;		stz	|cyareg		; slow down for this;;		ldy	#3		; delay to let the motor;@loop;		jsr	delay		;   come up to speed;		dey;		bne	@loop;;		jsr	chkdrv0		; see if the motor actually comes on;		php			; save status;		ply			; in Y register;		lda	|motoroff,x	; turn off motor;		pla			; restore speed register;		sta	|cyareg;		tya			; restore processor status into Accumulator;		bit	#%0000010	; check the Z flag;		rep	#$10		; back to 16-bit registers;		longi	on;		bne	no_device	; if motor not on, then no drive connected!;		;		plb			; restore my DBR;		ply			; and slot #** Correct the slot number in the DIB for internal/external.*		lda	>sltromsel		rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	oncheck_int_ext		lsr	a		dey		bpl	check_int_ext		bcc	not_ext_slot	; if not an external slot		ldy	#slot_num	; else update DIB		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		ora	#$0008		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],ynot_ext_slot		bit	|vbl_task_flag	; has task been installed?		bmi	task_already_in	; yes		pea	disk2_task>>16	; else install VBL task		pea	disk2_task		_setheartbeat		bcs	no_disk2	; if cant install task		pea	$0002		; enable VBL interrupts		_intsource		bcs	no_disk2	; if cant get interrupts startedtask_already_in		dec	|vbl_task_flag	; prevent redundant vbl installation** Now generate a unique name for the device.*		ldy	#dev_name+14	;'AppleDisk5.25A'		lda	|unique_name		sta	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		inc	|unique_name** Startup is complete.*		lda	#no_errordelay		clc		rts** Either the hardware was not found or the vbl task used to detect* disk switched status could not be installed.  In either case the* device will be purged.*no_device		plb			; restore DBR		ply			; clean up stackno_disk2		rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		lda	#drvr_no_dev	; return error to purge device		sec		rts		eject******************************************************************* This is the VBL task used to simulate disk switched errors.* If the counter maintained for a device is nonzero, then it* can be assumed that the device had a media access within the* last 1 second.  If the counter maintained for the device is* zero then the media has not been accessed within the last 1* second and it is assumed that a switch occured.  Counters are* preset to 60 (60 vbl cycles = 1 second) after a successful* media access and are decremented by the vbl task every vbl* if and only if the counters are nonzero.** Each timer is a word value but is limited to 0 through 60.** ENTRY: Call via 'JSL'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 1 1 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTL'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = Unchanged*               B Reg = Unchanged*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 1 1 0 x x x   0******************************************************************		entry	disk2_task		entry	task_counterdisk2_task		dc.l	0		; room for task header linktask_counter		dc.w	1		; call me every vbl		dc.b	$5A,$A5		; task signature word		longa	off		longi	off		phb		phk		plb		ldx	#(14*2)-2	; point at last disksw timernext_timer		lda	|dsw_timers,x		beq	dont_decr	; leave alone if already zero		dec	|dsw_timers,x	; else time down 1 seconddont_decr		dex		dex		bpl	next_timer	; check all 14 timers		inc	|task_counter	; reset task count for next vbl		plb		rtl		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  OPEN** This call opens a device in preparation for subsequent read* from or writes to the device.  The DISK][ driver is a block* device which does not support the open function and will* return with no error.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************open		PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on		entry	close,get_partition,dev_reset,media_eject,set_partn		entry	arm_event,disarm_event,set_partition,flush,set_format		entry	set_ctrlclose		get_partitiondev_resetmedia_ejectset_partnarm_eventdisarm_eventset_partitionflushset_formatset_ctrl		lda	#no_error	; and exit w/o error		clc		rts				ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  READ** This call executes a read from the device.  The DISK][ device* driver supports two different block and volume sizes:**               Block Size              Volume Size*                256 byte                560 block*                512 byte                280 block** The DIB is configured for the 512 byte 280 block format.  In* order to support DOS3.3 file system translators this driver* will interpret 256 byte access' as half block access'.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*       <drvr_buf_ptr = Pointer to I/O buffer*       <drvr_blk_num = Initial block number*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*      <drvr_blk_size = Size of block to be accessed*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************read		PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on** 		Precheck the request count for a request of $00000000.*		lda	<drvr_req_cnt		ora	<drvr_req_cnt+2		bne	not_null_req	;if something to do		lda	#no_error		clc		rts** 		Precheck the disk switch task counter for this device.* 		Preset counter to 60 after check regardless of result of check.* 		If check is zero then exit imeadiately with a disk switched error.*not_null_req		ldy	#driver_unit	; my internal unit number		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		asl	a		tax		lda	|dsw_timers,x	; get current disk switch status		bne	no_dsw_error	; ok to access device!		** Disk switch timer timed out.  Must be a disk switched error.* Preset the counter for next access prior to exit with error.*		lda	#$0004		; JOA 7/27/88		clc		jsr	set_dev_stat	;clear WP status (leave online???!)*		jsr	preset_dsw		lda	#drvr_disk_sw		sec		rts** No disk switch occured.  OK to complete read operation.*no_dsw_error		lda	#$0001		; set RWTS command: read		sta	|my_ibcmd		jsr	xlate_call	; translate to DISK][ call		bcc	next_blk_chk	; if no error		php		pha		cmp	#drvr_off_line	; is device offline?		bne	stat_done	; no		lda	#$0014		; clear online & WP status JOA 7/27/88		clc		jsr	set_dev_stat		stat_done	pla		plp		jsr	preset_dsw	; set disksw timer for next access		rts				next_blk_chk		** We know some things about the device status at this point.* Set Online and *wrprot.*		lda	#$0010		; set device online status		ora	|my_ibwpbit	; add in the WriteProt status if any		sec		jsr	set_dev_stat		lda	#$0001		; clear disksw status		clc		jsr	set_dev_stat		jsr	preset_dsw	; set disksw timer for next access		lda	#no_error	; else time to return		clc		rts		EndP		eject******************************************************************* This routine presets the disk switched counter for the* device currently being accessed.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Unchanged*               X Reg = driver_unit * 2*               Y Reg = DIB offset to driver_unit*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0  Status is unchanged******************************************************************preset_dsw	Proc		longa	on		longi	on		php		pha		ldy	#driver_unit	; my internal unit number		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		asl	a		tax		lda	#60		sta	|dsw_timers,x	; and preset for next access		pla		plp		rts		endp		eject******************************************************************* This routine will set the device status word maintained* internally by the driver.  Since there is no status call* to support the DISK][ device it is neccessary to update* the status word dynamically based on results from a device* access.  This indicates that the result of a status call will* be based on assumptions resulting from the last device access.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Bits to be set or reset in status word*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0 to clear status bits*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0 to set status bits** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Device Status Word*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0******************************************************************set_dev_stat	Proc		php		pha		ldy	#driver_unit	; internal device number		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		asl	a		tax		lda	|dstat_tbl,x		tax			; point at device status word		pla		plp		bcs	set_bits		eor	#$FFFF		; clear status bits		and	|0,x		sta	|0,x		rtsset_bits		ora	|0,x		; set bits		sta	|0,x		rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  WRITE** This call executes a read from the device.  The DISK][ device* driver supports two different block and volume sizes:**               Block Size              Volume Size*                256 byte                560 block*                512 byte                280 block** The DIB is configured for the 512 byte 280 block format.  In* order to support DOS3.3 file system translators this driver* will interpret 256 byte access' as half block access'.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*       <drvr_buf_ptr = Pointer to I/O buffer*       <drvr_blk_num = Initial block number*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*      <drvr_blk_size = Size of block to be accessed*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************write		PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on** Precheck the request count for a request of $00000000.*		lda	<drvr_req_cnt		ora	<drvr_req_cnt+2		bne	not_null_req		lda	#no_error		clc		rts** Precheck the disk switch task counter for this device.* Preset counter to 60 after check regardless of result of check.* If check is zero then exit imeadiately with a disk switched error.*not_null_req		ldy	#driver_unit	; my internal unit number		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		asl	a		tax		lda	|dsw_timers,x	; get current disk switch status		bne	no_dsw_error	; ok to access device!* added 7/27/88 JOA		lda	#$0004		clc		jsr	set_dev_stat	;clear WP bits (and leave ONLINE ???!)** Disk switch timer timed out.  Must be a disk switched error.* Preset the counter for next access prior to exit with error.*		jsr	preset_dsw		lda	#drvr_disk_sw		sec		rts** No disk switch occured.  OK to complete read operation.*no_dsw_error		lda	#$0002		; set RWTS command: write		sta	|my_ibcmd		jsr	xlate_call	; translate to DISK][ call		bcc	next_blk_chk	; if no error this block		php		pha		cmp	#drvr_off_line	; is device offline?		bne	not_off_line	; no		lda	#$0014		; clear online and WP bits		clc		jsr	set_dev_stat		bra	stat_donenot_off_line		cmp	#drvr_wr_prot	; is device write protected?		bne	stat_done	; no		lda	#$0004		; else set wrprot status		sec		jsr	set_dev_statstat_done		pla		plp		jsr	preset_dsw	; set disksw timer for next access		rtsnext_blk_chk** We know some things about the device status at this point.* Set Online and *wrprot.*		lda	#$0010		; set device online status		sec		jsr	set_dev_stat		lda	#$0005		; clear wrprot & disksw status		clc		jsr	set_dev_stat		jsr	preset_dsw	; set disksw timer for next access		lda	#no_error	; else time to return		clc		rts				ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  STATUS** This routine supports all the standard device status calls.* Any status call which is able to detect an OFFLINE or DISK* SWITCHED condition should call the system service routine* SET_DISKSW.  OFFLINE and DISKSW are conditions and not errors* when detected by a status call and should only be returned as* conditions in the status list.** Status Code:  $0000   Return Device Status*               $0001   Return Control Parameters*               $0002   Return Wait/No Wait Mode*               $0003   Return Format Options*               $0004   Return Parition Map** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_clist_ptr = Pointer to control list*     <drvr_ctrl_code = Control code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************status		PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on** Need to verify that the status code specifies a* legal status request.*		lda	<drvr_stat_code	; is this a legal status request?		bmi	dev_specific	; could be, it's device specific		cmp	#$0005		blt	legal_status	; yesbad_code_err		lda	#drvr_bad_code	; else return 'BAD CODE' error		rts** It's a legal status.  Dispatch to the appropriate status routine.*legal_status		asl	a		tax 		jmp	(|status_table,x)dev_specific	cmp	#$8001		; return volume #?		sec			; assume error (pessimists, ain't we?)		bne	bad_code_err	; no...		jmp	get_wait	; else go "borrow" some code		eject******************************************************************* The DEVICE STATUS call returns a status list that indicates* specific status information regarding a character of block* device and the total number of blocks supported by a block device.** Status List Pointer:  Word            General status word*                       Longword        Total number of blocks** Encoding of status for a block device is as follows:*  ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___ ___* |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |* | F | E | D | C | B | A | 9 | 8 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 4 | 3 | 2 | 1 | 0 |* |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |__ DISK SW*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |______ INTERRUPT*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |__________ WRITE PROT*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |______________ 0 RESERVED*   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |__________________ ONLINE*   |   |___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|___|______________________ 0 RESERVED*   |______________________________________________________________ BLK FLAG** Valid request counts versus returned status list for this status* call are as follows:** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_slist_ptr = Pointer to status list*     <drvr_stat_code = Status code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred (2 - 6)*               A Reg = Status code * 2*               X Reg = Status code * 2*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************		entry	dev_statdev_stat		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#drvr_bad_parm	; assume invalid request count		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt+2	; and validate request count		bne	bad_dev_stat		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt		cpx	#$0002		blt	bad_dev_stat		cpx	#$0007		blt	ok_dev_statbad_dev_stat		sec		rts** Request count is valid.  Deterime device status and if appropriate, the* total number of blocks for the device and return them in the device* status list.  You insert the code required for this operation.*ok_dev_stat		ldy	#driver_unit	; internal device #		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		asl	a		tax* added 7/27/88        JOA		lda	|dsw_timers,x	;should offline be the state  ?		bne	no_dsw_err	;no.		phx		lda	#$0004		;be sure WP status is off		clc		jsr	set_dev_stat	;clear WP status bits (leave online??!)		plx*no_dsw_err	lda	|dstat_tbl,x	; get pointer to device status list		tax** Get default block count from DIB.*		ldy	#blk_cnt		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		sta	|2,x		iny		iny		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		sta	|4,x** If it's a DOS3.3 access then the block count in the DIB is half* of the actual block count for the block size accessed by the* DOS3.3 file system translator.*		lda	<drvr_blk_size	; is this a DOS3.3 access?		cmp	#256		bne	not_sos_stat	; no		lda	|2,x		; else double the block count!		asl	a		sta	|2,x		lda	|4,x		rol	a		sta	|4,xnot_sos_stat		phx			; save offset		lda	#0		; clear accumulator		sep	#$20		; go to 8-bit accumulator		longa	off		ldy	#slot_num	; get the slot number		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		pha			; save for a minute		and	#$07		; make into 0-7		asl	a		; make into $x0		asl	a		asl	a		asl	a		tax			; into X		ldy	#unit_num	; check drive 1 or drive 2		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		dec	a		; is it drive 1?		beq	@drive_1	; yes, select it		lda	>drv1en,x	; else select drive 2		bra	@selected@drive_1		lda	>drv0en,x@selected		pla			; retrieve slot number		bit	#%00001000	; internal?		bne	@external	; no, must be Disk][ controller		lda	>q7l,x		; ensure read mode (not write)		lda	>q6h,x		; prepare to read status		lda	>q7l,x		; read it		tay			; save in Y		bit	#%00100000	; motor still on?		bne	@store_wp	; yes, wp status is valid		lda	>q7h,x		; prepare to set mode		lda	#%00000100	; turn off 1 second motor-off timer		sta	>q6h,x		lda	>q6l,x		lda	>q7l,x		; make sure write mode is off		lda	>motoron,x	; motor on		lda	>q6h,x		; sense write protect		lda	>q7l,x		tay			; save status		lda	>motoroff,x	; motor off@wait		lda	>q6h,x		; wait for the motor to go off		lda	>q7l,x		bit	#%00100000		bne	@wait		lda	>q7h,x		lda	#$00		; turn timer back on		sta	>q6h,x		lda	>q6l,x		; leave everything in a safe mode		lda	>q7l,x		bra	@store_wp	; go store the write protect bit@external		lda	>motoron,x	; motor on		lda	>q6h,x		; sense write protect		lda	>q7l,x		tay			; save status		lda	>motoroff,x	; motor off@store_wp		plx			; retrieve internal status index		tya			; retrieve status		asl	a		; bit 7 -> carry		lda	#$00		; clear accumulator		rol	a		; carry -> bit 0		asl	a		; bit 0 -> bit 1		asl	a		; bit 1 -> bit 2		pha			; save for a bit		lda	|0,x		; get status		and	#%11111011	; clear write-protect bit		ora	1,s		; and set to real status		sta	|0,x		; store again		pla			; clean up stack** Now copy the internal status list to the destination* status list specified in the call parameters.*		ldy	#$0000		; status list pointercopy_dstat		lda	|0,x		; copy device status list to slist_ptr		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr],y		inx		iny		cpy	<drvr_req_cnt	; copy = request count size		bne	copy_dstat		rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on** After returning the device status list check for an OFFLINE* or DISKSW state.  If either of these conditions exist then* the driver must call SET_DISKSW via the system service call* table.*		ldy	#driver_unit	; internal device #		lda	<drvr_blk_size	; is this a 512 byte access?		cmp	#512		beq	dont_set_bf	; yes, block count is valid!		cmp	#256		; is this a 256 byte access?		beq	dont_set_bf	; yes, block count is valid!		lda	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		ora	#$8000		; dont know if block count is valid!		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr]dont_set_bf		lda	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		eor	#$0010		; convert online to offline		and	#$0011		; offline or disk switched?		beq	not_blk_stat	; no		jsl	set_disksw	; else call system servicenot_blk_stat		brl	set_xfer_cnt	; update xfer count & exit		eject******************************************************************* This call returns a byte count as the first word in the status* list followed by the data from the configuration parameter list.* The request count specifies how much data is to be returned* from the list.  If the byte count is smaller than the request* count then only the number of bytes specified by the byte* count will be returned and the transfer count will indicate* this.** Status List:  Word    Number of bytes in configuration list (including byte count).*               Data    Data from the configuration list (device specific).** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_slist_ptr = Pointer to status list*     <drvr_stat_code = Status code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred (2 - $FFFF)*               A Reg = Status code * 2*               X Reg = Status code * 2*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************		entry	get_ctrlget_ctrl		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#drvr_bad_parm		; assume invalid request count		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt+2		; and validate request count		bne	bad_get_ctrl		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt		cpx	#$0002		bge	ok_get_ctrlbad_get_ctrl		sec		rts** Request count is valid.  Return control list.*ok_get_ctrl		lda	#$0000			; no control list this device		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr]				sta	<drvr_tran_cnt+2	; transfer count always $00000002		lda	#$0002		sta	<drvr_tran_cnt		lda	#no_error		clc		rts		eject******************************************************************* This routine returns the Wait/No Wait mode that the driver* is currently operating in.  This is returned in a word* parameter which indicates a request count of $0002.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_slist_ptr = Pointer to status list*     <drvr_stat_code = Status code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred (2)*               A Reg = Status code * 2*               X Reg = Status code * 2*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************		entry	get_waitget_wait		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#drvr_bad_parm	; assume invalid request count		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt+2	; and validate request count		bne	bad_get_wait		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt		cpx	#$0002		beq	ok_get_waitbad_get_wait		sec		rts** Request count is valid. Return the wait mode for this device.*ok_get_wait		lda	#$0000		; block devices always in wait mode		ldx	drvr_stat_code	; is this a get_wait_mode or get_vol_num call?		bpl	set_slist_field	; get_wait_mode, go ahead and return		lda	|my_volume	; get the last volume number returned by a RWTS call		and	#$00FF		; low byte onlyset_slist_field		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		brl	set_xfer_cnt		eject******************************************************************* This routine returns the format options for the device.* Consult the driver specification for the format option list.* This call requires a minimum request count of $00000002.  The* maximum request count may exceed the size of the format list* in which case the request count returned will indicate the* size of the format list.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_slist_ptr = Pointer to status list*     <drvr_stat_code = Status code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred (2 - n)*               A Reg = Status code * 2*               X Reg = Status code * 2*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************		entry	get_formatget_format		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#drvr_bad_parm	; assume invalid request count		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt+2	; and validate request count		bne	bad_get_format		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt		cpx	#$0002		bge	ok_get_formatbad_get_format		sec		rts** Request count is valid. Return the format options for this device.*ok_get_format		ldx	#format_tbl	; point at format options list		lda	|0,x		; get # entries in option list		asl	a		; list length = (n * 16) + 8		asl	a		asl	a		asl	a		clc		adc	#$0008		; now have option list length		cmp	<drvr_req_cnt	; is request longer then list length?		bge	req_count_ok		sta	<drvr_req_cntreq_count_ok		ldy	#$0000		; status list index		sep	#$20		; 8 bit 'm'		longa	offcopy_format		lda	|0,x		; copy format option list to slist_ptr		sta	[<drvr_slist_ptr],y		inx		iny		cpy	<drvr_req_cnt	; copy = request count size		bne	copy_format		rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		brl	set_xfer_cnt		eject******************************************************************* This is a common exit routine for successful status calls.* The transfer count is set to the same value as the request* count prior to returning with no error.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred (2 - 6)*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code = No Error*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error******************************************************************		entry	set_xfer_cntset_xfer_cnt		longa	on		longi	on		lda	<drvr_req_cnt	; set transfer count		sta	<drvr_tran_cnt		lda	<drvr_req_cnt+2		sta	<drvr_tran_cnt+2		lda	#no_error		clc		rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  CONTROL** This routine supports all the standard device control calls.** Control Code: $0000   Reset Device*               $0001   Format Device*               $0002   Eject Media*               $0003   Set Control Parameters*               $0004   Set Wait/No Wait Mode*               $0005   Set Format Options*               $0006   Assign Partition Owner*               $0007   Arm Event*               $0008   Disarm Event*               $0009   Set Partition Map** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_clist_ptr = Pointer to control list*     <drvr_ctrl_code = Control code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************control		PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on** Need to verify that the control code specifies a* legal control request.*		lda	<drvr_stat_code	; is this a legal control request?		bmi	dev_specific		cmp	#$000A		blt	legal_control	; yesbad_code		lda	#drvr_bad_code	; else return 'BAD CODE' error		rts** It's a legal control.  Dispatch to the appropriate control routine.*legal_control		asl	a		tax 		jmp	(|control_table,x)dev_specific		cmp	#$8001		; only device specific call we have!		sec			; assume error		bne	bad_code	; return error		brl	set_volnum	; go ahead and set the volume number		eject******************************************************************* This routine will physically format the media.  No additional* information associated with any particular file system will* be written to the media. Check task count for disk switch* prior to  execution of read.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_clist_ptr = Pointer to control list*     <drvr_ctrl_code = Control code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*               A Reg = Control code * 2*               X Reg = Control code * 2*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************		entry	formatformat		longa	on		longi	on				lda	|format_volnum	; get the desired volume number		sta	|rwts_volnum	; set to pass to RWTS		stz	|format_volnum	; reset it		lda	#$0003		; set RWTS command: format		sta	|my_ibcmd		jmp	xlate_call		eject******************************************************************* This routine will set the WAIT/NO WAIT mode as specified* by the contents of the control list.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_clist_ptr = Pointer to control list*     <drvr_ctrl_code = Control code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*               A Reg = Control code * 2*               X Reg = Control code * 2*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************		entry	set_waitset_wait		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#drvr_bad_parm	; assume invalid request count		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt+2	; and validate request count		bne	bad_set_wait		ldx	<drvr_req_cnt		cpx	#$0002		beq	ok_set_waitbad_set_wait		sec		rts** Request count is valid. Set the wait mode for this device.*ok_set_wait		lda	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		beq	wait_mode_ok		lda	#drvr_bad_parm		sec		rtswait_mode_ok		brl	set_xfer_cnt		eject******************************************************************* This routine will set the volume # to be used in the next Format* call.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*     <drvr_clist_ptr = Pointer to control list*     <drvr_ctrl_code = Control code*       <drvr_req_cnt = Number of bytes to be transferred*               A Reg = $8001*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************set_volnum		longa	on		longi	on		ldx	#drvr_bad_parm	; assume invalid request count		lda	<drvr_req_cnt+2	; and validate request count		bne	oops		lda	<drvr_req_cnt		cmp	#$0002		beq	ok_set_numoops		txa			; put error code into Acc		sec		rts** Request count is valid. Set the volume number for the next format.*ok_set_num		ldx	#drvr_bad_parm	; assume bad volume number		lda	[<drvr_slist_ptr]		cmp	#255		; volume number in range?		bge	oops		; no...		sta	|format_volnum		brl	set_xfer_cnt		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER CALL:  SHUTDOWN** This call prepares the driver for shutdown.  This may include* closing a character device as well as releasing any and all* system resources that may have been aquired by either a* STARTUP or OPEN call.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*       <drvr_dev_num = Device Number of current device being accessed*               A Reg = Call Number*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Undefined*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*      <drvr_tran_cnt = Number of bytes transferred*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Same as entry*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  if no error*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  if error******************************************************************shutdn		PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on		inc	|vbl_task_flag	; should task be removed?		bpl	@do_shutdown	; yes, continue		lda	#drvr_busy	; not until last device is shutdown		sec			; busy if task left in		rts@do_shutdown		pea	disk2_task>>16	; else remove task		pea	disk2_task		_delheartbeat; now we reinitialize the modified data in preparation for a warm restart		ldx	#(14*2)-2	; 14 devices@loop1		stz	|dsw_timers,x	; zero the disk switched timers		dex		dex		bpl	@loop1		stz	|access_flag		lda	#' A'		; bytes will be reversed when stored		sta	|unique_name		stz	|disk2_task	; reinit the hearbeat task header		stz	|disk2_task+2		lda	#1		sta	|task_counter		; reinit the device status table		phb			; save DBR (mvn changes it)		lda	#xtra_dstat_end-xtra_dstat1-1		ldx	#xtra_dstat1		ldy	#dstat1		mvn	xtra_dstat1,dstat1		plb		lda	#no_error	; no error if task left in		clc		rtsxtra_dstat1	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat2	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat3	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat4	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat5	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat6	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat7	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat8	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat9	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstatA	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstatB	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstatC	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstatD	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstatE	dc.b	$10,$00		; device general status word		dc.l	280		; device block countxtra_dstat_end		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* This routine will translate the GS/OS device call into* a format compatable with the existing SOS Disk Driver core* routines and execute the device access.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  If no error occured.*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  If error occured.******************************************************************xlate_call	PROC					;using   driver_data		longa	on		longi	on		pei	<drvr_blk_num	;save for later restoring		sep	#$20		; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		lda	>cyareg				pha			; save for now		lda	#$80		; fast speed and no motor on detect		sta	>cyareg				lda	>statereg		pha		ora	#%00000100	; switch LC to right side		sta	>statereg		rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		lda	<drvr_call_num	; is this a control call?		cmp	#drvr_control		beq	xlate1		; yes, dont care about parameters		lda	<drvr_blk_size		cmp	#512		; is it a standard block access?		beq	xlate0		; yes				cmp	#256		; is this a DOS3.3 access?		beq	xlate2		; yes		ldx	#drvr_bad_parm	; can't deal with any other block sizeerror_exit		sep	#$20		; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		pla		sta	>statereg				pla		sta	>cyareg		rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		pla		sta	<drvr_blk_num		txa			; return error in accumulator		sec		rts** must validate the request count to ensure it's a multiple of the block size*xlate0		ldx	#drvr_bad_count	; assume error		lda	<drvr_req_cnt	; get the request count		and	#$01FF		; MOD with block size		bne	error_exit	; if remainder, bad request count** For a standard access, double the block address and read two 256 byte* sectors for each block requested.*xlate1		asl	<drvr_blk_num		rol	<drvr_blk_num+2		bra	xlate3** For DOS3.3 access of the device, only 256 byte blocks are allowed.* In this case, the device supports 560 blocks total. Save absolute zero page.*xlate2		ldx	#drvr_bad_count	; assume error		lda	<drvr_req_cnt	; get the request count		and	#$00FF		; MOD with block size		bne	error_exit	; if remainder, bad request countxlate3;		save the absolute zero page. 		phb			; save DBR		lda	#zp_size-1	; init count		ldx	#0		; init source (absolute zero page)		ldy	#azp_save	; init destination		mvn	0,azp_save	; do the move		plb			; restore DBR** Set flag to indicate that this is either a 256 byte or 512 byte access.*		lda	<drvr_blk_size		xba		sta	|access_flag** Validate block prior to device access*				xlate5				 ** Translate GS/OS Driver Call to RWTS Call.*		sep	#$20		; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		ldy	#dib_pro_unit		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		and	#%01110000		sta	|my_ibslot	; set slot * 16		ldy	#unit_num		lda	[<drvr_dib_ptr],y		sta	|my_ibdrvn	; set drive #		lda	#$01		sta	|my_ibtype	; RWTS IOB		lda	|rwts_volnum	; copy the requested volume # to IOB		sta	|my_ibvol		stz	|rwts_volnum	; reset for next access		rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		jsr	check_block		bcc	xlate5a		; if ok				jmp	xlate8a		; return with bad block number error				xlate5a		lda	<drvr_blk_num	; validate block number		lsr	a		; block number / 16 = track		lsr	a		lsr	a		lsr	a		sep	#$20		; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		sta	|my_ibtrk	; track  = quotient:  block / 16;		set the initial buffer pointer.		rep	#$20		longa	on		lda	<drvr_buf_ptr		sta	my_ibbufp		lda	<drvr_buf_ptr+2		sta	my_ibbufp+2** 		Copy our IOB to bank $00 for RWTS routines.*		phb			; save DBR		lda	#$14-1		; init count		ldx	#my_iob		; init source		ldy	#ibtype		; init destination		mvn	my_iob,ibtype	; do the move		plb			; restore DBR** Copy nibblizing tables to bank $00*		pea	my_dnibl>>16	; source buffer		pea	my_dnibl		pea	dnibl_dest>>16	; destination buffer		pea	dnibl_dest		pea	$0000		; block size		pea	$0200		pea	move_sinc_dinc	; src incr & dest incr		jsl	move_info						rep	#$20		; 16 bit 'm'		longa	on		lda	<drvr_buf_ptr+1		sta	tk_base				lda	<drvr_req_cnt+1		sta	secleft		; # of sectors left				lda	<drvr_blk_num	; sector = remainder: block / 16		and	#$0F		sta	|lowsc		;		start of main loop for each track.		xlate5d		lda	secleft		clc		adc	lowsc		bcs	xlate6		; if it actually wrapped		dea		cmp	#15+1		bcc	xlate7		; if doesn't extend into next trackxlate6		lda	#15xlate7		sta	highsc		; high sector on this track		sec		sbc	lowsc		ina		sta	nsec		; # of sectors to read on this track		sta	nsec2;		init the sector map for this track.		ldx	#16-1-1xlate7a		stz	Tscmap,x		dex		dex		bpl	xlate7a		; if more to clear		* 		Call RWTS for device access.		phd		phb 		lda	#0		; clear accumulator		tcd			; set direct register to absolute zero page		sep	#$30		; 8 bit 'm' & 'x'		longa	off		longi	off		pha			; put #0 on stack...		plb			; to set DBR to bank 0				jsr	rwts1		; call read/write track sector		rep	#$30		; 16 bit 'm' & 'x'		longa	on		longi	on				plb		pld** Update our IOB with the results from the call to RWTS.*		phb			; save DBR		lda	#$14-1		; init counter		ldx	#ibtype		; init source pointer		ldy	#my_iob		; init destination pointer		mvn	ibtype,my_iob	; do the move		plb			; restore DBR** Need to keep my current track, prior etc...*		pea	curtrk>>16	; source buffer		pea	curtrk		pea	my_curtrk>>16	; destination buffer		pea	my_curtrk		pea	$0000		; block size		pea	$0019		pea	move_sinc_dinc	; src incr & dest incr		jsl	move_info		lda	<drvr_call_num		cmp	#drvr_control	; is this a control (format)?		beq	exit_time	; yes						lda	nsec2		sec		sbc	nsec		; # left to read on track		sta	>w1		; save sectors transferred for now		lda	<drvr_tran_cnt+1		clc		adc	>w1		sta	<drvr_tran_cnt+1		cmp	<drvr_req_cnt+1		bcs	exit_time	; if done						lda	|my_ibstat		and	#$ff		bne	exit_time	; if got an error		;		process next track.						lda	tk_base		clc		adc	nsec2		; # of sectors read off this track		sta	tk_base						lda	my_ibtrk	; get track and sector		and	#$ff		; remove sector information		ina		cmp	#34+1		bcc	xlate9		; if haven't hit end of disk		xlate8a		lda	#drvr_bad_block				sep	#$20		sta	|my_ibstat		rep	#$20		bra	exit_timexlate9		shortm		sta	|my_ibtrk		sta	>ibtrk		longm				stz	lowsc		; start at begining of track		lda	secleft		sec		sbc	>w1		sta	secleft				jmp	xlate5d		; process next track		*	 Restore absolute zero page.exit_time 		phb			; save DBR		lda	#zp_size-1	; init count		ldx	#azp_save	; init source pointer		ldy	#0		; init destination pointer (absolute zero page)		mvn	azp_save,0	; do the move		plb			; restore DBR 		inc	a		; make accumulator = 0 (was $FFFF after MVN operation)		sep	#$20		; 8 bit 'm'		longa	off		pla		sta	>statereg	; restore original hardware state		pla		sta	>cyareg				plx		stx	<drvr_blk_num		lda	|my_ibstat	; accumulator is still 8-bits wide here		rep	#$20		; shift back to 16-bits		longa	on		cmp	#$0001		; condition carry status from error code in accumulator		rts		eject******************************************************************* Validate the block number and block size.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x x   0** EXIT: via an 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*             Dir Reg = GS/OS Direct Page*               B Reg = Current program bank*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C   E*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 0   0  If no error occured.*                       x x 0 0 0 x x 1   0  If error occured.******************************************************************		entry	check_blockcheck_block		longa	on		longi	on		lda	<drvr_call_num	; is it a read or write call?		cmp	#drvr_read		beq	chk_blk_now	; yes		cmp	#drvr_write		bne	in_range	; nochk_blk_now		lda	<drvr_blk_num+2		bne	ret_bad_blk		lda	<drvr_blk_num		cmp	#560		; is the block number in range?		bge	ret_bad_blk	; no...** Block number is in range.  Go ahead and read it.*in_range		lda	#no_error		clc		rts		ret_bad_blk		lda	#drvr_bad_block	; cant deal with this block number		sec		rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER SUBROUTINE: RWTS1** NOTE:  Critical timing requires page bound considerations*        for code and data.  Vertually the entire WRITE routine*        must not cross page boundaries.  Critical branches in*        the WRITE, READ and READADDR subroutines which must not*        cross page boundaries are noted in comment fields.**               35 tracks*               16 sectors per track*              256 bytes per sector** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed = 1 mHz*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*              <slotz = Slot * 16** EXIT: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error******************************************************************rwts1		PROC		entry	drivsel		entry	drvwait		entry	ok		entry	ok1		entry	motof		entry	trytrk		entry	trytrk2		entry	tryadr		entry	tryadr2		entry	rdright		entry	recal1		entry	alldone					;using   driver_data		entry	rttrk		longa	off		longi	off				php			; save interrupt state		lda	1,s		sta	<irqmask		jsr	rsetphse	; reset phase lines		lda	|q7l,x		; turn off write enable		jsr	rwts2		plp			; restore interrupt state		rtsrwts2		ldy	#1		; retry count		sty	|seekcnt	; only one recalibrate per call		jsr	chkprev		; make all drives are stopped.** 		Now check if the motor is on, then start it*		jsr	chkdrv		; set zero flag if motor stopped		php			; save test results		lda	#dvmot		sta	|montimeh		lda	<ibdrvn		; determine drive 1 or 2		cmp	<iobpdn		; same drive used before?		sta	<iobpdn		; save it for next time		php			; keep results of compare		lda	<ibslot		; determine slot number		cmp	<iobpsn		; same slot used before?		sta	<iobpsn		; save it for next time		beq	slot_ok		php		pla		sta	1,sslot_ok		lda	<ibdrvn		; get drive number into carry		dec	a		ror	a		lda	|motoron,x	; turn on the drive		bcc	drivsel		; if drive 1		inx			; else drive 2drivsel		lda	|drv0en,x		plp			; was it same drive?		beq	ok		plp			; Indicate drive off in Z flag		ldy	#$07		; delay 150 mSec before steppingdrvwait		jsr	mswait		; (on return A=0)		dey		bne	drvwait		php			; now zero flag setok		lda	<ibcmd		; make sure this command needs seeked.		beq	ok1		; if status check.		cmp	#$03		; format does not need seeked either		beq	ok1		lda	<ibtrk		; get destination track				jsr	myseek		; and go to it.** Now R/W head is at the desired track.  Was the motor on to start with?*ok1		plp			; was motor on?		bne	trytrk		; if so, dont delay** Motor was off, wait for it to speed up.*motof		lda	#1		; Wait 100uS per count in montime		jsr	mswait				lda	|montimeh			bmi	motof		; count up to zero** Motor should be up to speed.  If it still looks stopped then* the drive is not present.*		jsr	chkdrv		; is drive present?				bne	trytrk0		;if drive is present				jmp	hndlerr		; handle error of drive not being found		* 		code to return ibwpbit added 7/27/88 JOAtrytrk0		stz	ibwpbit		;assume its not WP		lda	|q6h,x		;go to sense mode		lda	|q7l,x		;get the sense status		bit	|q6l,x		;reset to read mode		rol	a		;carry set if WP is true		bcc	trytrk		;forget it				lda	#$04		sta	ibwpbit		;return an 0004** 		Now check if it is not the format disk command, locate the correct* 		sector for this operation.*trytrk		lda	<ibcmd		; get command code #		bne	trytrk1		; if not status command		jmp	statcmd		; try status command		trytrk1		cmp	#$03		; is it a format?		bne	not_format	; no		jmp	format_media	; else go format medianot_format		lsr	a		; set carry=1 for read, 0 for write		bcs	trytrk2		; must prenibblize for write.				lda	#$ff		sta	>nxtwrt				trytrk2		ldy	#$40		; only 64 retries of any kind		sty	retrycnttryadr		ldx	<ibslot		; get slot num into x-reg		jsr	rdadr16		; read next address field		bcc	rdright		; if read it right, hurrah!		tryadr2		dec	|retrycnt	; another mistake!!		bpl	tryadr		; well, let it go this time.,				lda	#drvr_io_error	; anticipate a bad drive error		dec	|seekcnt	; only recalibrate once!		bmi	hndlerr		; tried ot recalibrate too many times				lda	|curtrk		pha			; save track we really want		lda	#40		; pretent we are on track 40		ldy	#$40		sty	|retrycnt	; reset retrys to 64 max.		bne	recal1		; branch always * * have now read an address field correctly.* make sure this is the track, sector, and volume desired.*rdright		ldy	|track		; on the right track?		cpy	|curtrk				beq	rttrk		; if so, good** 		recalibrating from this track*		lda	|curtrk		; preserve destination track		pha		tya			asl	a		; (washing machine fix!)		jsr	settrk		bra	junk		recal1		jsr	settrk		jsr	myseek				junk		pla		jsr	myseek				lda	#$80		sta	>cyareg		lda	<irqmask		pha		plp			; allow any pending interrupts		sei			; close interrupt window		bra	tryadr		; try again		* 		drive is on right track		rttrk		lda	<ibcmd		; read or write?		lsr	a		; the carry will tell.		bcc	writ		; carry was set for read operation,		jsr	cbl		; compute buffer location		bcc	rttrk1		; if wanted				lda	<irqmask		pha		plp			; allow any pending interrupts		sei			; close interrupt window		bra	tryadr2		rttrk1		ldx	<ibslot		jsr	read16		; read the data field		bcs	tryadr2		; if got an errorrttrk2		lda	#$80		sta	>cyareg		jsr	mts		; mark this sector		beq	alldone		; if done		jmp	tryadralldone		lda	#no_error	; no error		dc.b	$d0		; branch never (skip 1 byte)hndlerr		sec			; indicate an error		aldone1		sta	<ibstat		; give him error#		php			; save error		lda	<irqmask		pha		plp			; allow any pending interrupts		sei			; close interrupt window		plp				ldx	<ibslot		; get the slot offset		lda	|motoroff,x	; turn drive off				rts			; all finished! writ		lda	sect		cmp	>nxtwrt				beq	writ2		;if set to write this sector		tax		lda	>nxtwrt		sta	w1		writ1		inx		txa		and	#$f		;make sure in range		sta	>nxtwrt		tax		jsr	cblE		;compute buffer location		bcs	writ1		;if we aren't interested in this sector				jsr	pdf		;prenibblize data bufferwrit1a		jmp	tryadr2		;this prevents infinite waiting		writ2		jsr	write16		; write nybbles now		bcs	stat2		jmp	rttrk2				statcmd		ldx	<ibslot		lda	|q6h,x		; test for write protected. 		lda	|q7l,x		rol	a		; write protect-->carry-->bit 0=1		lda	|q6l,x		; keep in read mode...		stat2		bcc	alldone		lda	#drvr_wr_prot	; disk is write protected!!		bne	hndlerr		; branch always 		longa 	off				eject******************************************************************* MYSEEK: Seek to the desired track** Seeks track 'n' in slot #x/$10* if drivno is negative, on drive 0* if drivno is positive, on drive 1** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Destination track*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed = 1 mHz*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*              <ibtrk = Destination track #*              <ibsec = Destination sector #*             <ibslot = Slot * 16** EXIT: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error*             <ibstat = error code******************************************************************		entry	myseekmyseek		entry	alloff		entry	nxoff		longa	off		longi	off		asl	a		; assume two phase stepper.		sta	|track		; save destination track(*2)				lda	#$0		sta	>cyareg		; make sure slow				jsr	alloff		; turn all phases off to be sure.		jsr	drvindx		; get index to previous track for drive		lda	>drv0trk,x		sta	|curtrk		; this is where i am		lda	|track		; and where i'm going to		sta	>drv0trk,x		jsr	seek		; go there!alloff		ldy	#3		; turn off all phases before returningnxoff		tya			; (send phase in acc.)		jsr	clrphase	; carry is clear, phases shold be turned off		dey		bpl	nxoff		lsr	|curtrk		; divide back down				lda	#$80		sta	>cyareg		; reset to fast speed		clc		rts			; all off... now it's dark		ENDP		EJECT*******************************************************************  Fast Seek Subroutine:** Waveform shown is a seek from track 0 to track 9.  Even tracks* appear under phase 0 while odd tracks appear under phase 2.*             ___         ___         ___         ___* P3 ________|11m|_______|9m |_______|9m |_______|11m|_______________*          ___         ___         ___         ___         ________* P2 _____|13m|_______|9m |_______|9m |_______|10m|_______|   36m  |_*       ___         ___         ___         ___         ___* P1 __|16m|_______|9m |_______|9m |_______|9m |_______|10m|_________*                ___         ___         ___         ___* P0 ___________|10m|_______|9m |_______|9m |_______|12m|____________** TRK.......1.....2.....3.....4.....5.....6.....7.....8.....9........** The last phase asserted must be on for an additional 25mS to allow* for read/write head settling.  Each phase assertion is overlapped* for approximately the final third of it's phase assertion by the* next phase assertion.  Phase lines are off before and after the seek.* The spindle motor should be on for a minimum of 150mS prior to* initiating the seek operation.** Entry: via a 'JSR'*              curtrk = current half track*               A Reg = Desired halftrack (single phase)*               X Reg = Slot number * 16*               Y Reg = undefined*               B Reg = Current program Bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1** ExIt: via a 'RTS'*              curtrk = final halftrack*               prior = last halftrack if seek was required*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Unchanged*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program Bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error**  montimel and montimeh are incremented by the number of 100 usec quantums*  required by seek for motor on time overlap.** --- variables used ---**  curtrk, trkn, count, prior, slottemp, montimel, montimeh******************************************************************seek		PROC		entry	clrphase					;using   driver_data		longa	off		longi	off		sta	|trkn		; save target track		cmp	|curtrk		; on desired track?		beq	setphase	; yes,energize phase and return		lda	#$0		sta	|trkcnt		; halftrack count.seek2		lda	|curtrk		; save curtrk for		sta	|prior		; delayed turnoff.		sec		sbc	|trkn		; delta-tracks.		beq	seekend		; br if curtrk=destination		bcs	out		; (move out, not in)		eor	#$FF		; calc trks to go.		inc	|curtrk		; incr current track (in).		bcc	mintst		; (always taken)out		adc	#$FE		; calc trks to go.		dec	|curtrk		; decr current track (out).mintst		cmp	|trkcnt		bcc	maxtst		;  and 'trks moved'.		lda	|trkcntmaxtst		cmp	#$9		bcs	step2		; if trkcnt>$8 leave y alone (y=$8).		tay			; else set acceleration index in y		secstep2		jsr	setphase		phx		tyx		lda	>ontable,x	; for 'ontime'.		plx		jsr	mswait		; (100 usec intervals)		lda	|prior		clc			; for phaseoff		jsr	clrphase	; turn off prior phase		phx		tyx		lda	>offtable,x	;  then wait 'offtime'.		plx		jsr	mswait		; (100 usec intervals)		inc	|trkcnt		;  'tracks moved' count.		bne	seek2		; (always taken)seekend		jsr	mswait		; settle 25 msec		clc			; set for phase offsetphase	lda	|curtrk		; get current trackclrphase		and	#3		; mask for 1 of 4 phases		rol	a		; double for phaseon/off index		ora	<ibslot				tax		lda	|phaseoff,x	; turn on/off one phase		ldx	<ibslot		; restore x-reg		rts			; and return		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* MSWAIT Subroutine** Delays a specified number of 100 usec intervals for motor on timing.           ** Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Number of 100uS intervals to delay*               X Reg = Slot number * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program Bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed is unknown.*            IWM Mode = Read mode** ExIt: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = $00*               X Reg = $00*               Y Reg = Unchanged*               B Reg = Current Program Bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1******************************************************************mswait		PROC		entry	msw1		entry	msw2					;using   driver_data		longa	off		longi	off		tax			; save for now		lda	#0		sta	>cyareg		; make sure slow				txa			; restore count				ldx	#$11msw1		dex			; delay 86 usec.		bne	msw1		inc	|montimel		bne	msw2		; double-byte		inc	|montimeh	; increment.msw2		sec		sbc	#$1		; done 'n' intervals?		bne	mswait		; if not.  Don't cross Page Boundary				lda	#$80		sta	>cyareg		; reset to fast				lda	#0				longa	on		longi	on				rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* This subroutine detects if the motor is stopped.  If motor is* stopped, controller's shift reg will not be changing.** Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*               Speed = 1 mhz** Exit: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = $00 if stopped*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 1 x  1  if stopped*                       x x 1 1 0 1 0 x  1  if not stopped******************************************************************chkdrv		PROC		entry	chkdrv0		entry	ckdrts					;using   driver_data		longa	off		longi	off		ldx	<ibslot		lda	#0		sta	>cyareg		; reset to slow modechkdrv0		longa	off		longi	off		ldy	#0		; init loop counterchkdrv1		lda	|q6l,x		; read the shift reg		jsr	ckdrts		; delay		pha		pla			; more delay		cmp	|q6l,x		; has shift reg changed?		bne	chkdrv2		; if motor is running		lda	#drvr_off_line	; anticipate error.		dey			; no,dec retry counter		bne	chkdrv1		; and try 256 times		chkdrv2		php			; save error flag		pha		lda	#$80		sta	>cyareg		; reset to fast speed		pla		plp			; restore error flag		ckdrts		rts			; then return		eject******************************************************************* Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*               Speed = 1 mhz** ExIt: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Unchanged*               X Reg = Slot * 2*               Y Reg = Unchanged*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 1 0  1  if drive 0*                       x x 1 1 0 1 0 1  1  if drive 1******************************************************************		entry	drvindxdrvindx		longa	off		longi	off		pha			; preserve acc.		clc		lda	<ibdrvn		; drive ($01 or $02)		dec	a		; drive now ($00 or $01)		ror	a		php			; carry = drive #		ror	a		; drive to bit 7		clc		adc	<ibslot		; bits 4-6 are slot #		lsr	a		lsr	a		lsr	a		lsr	a		tax			; into x for index to table		plp		pla			; restore acc.		rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* Read address field subroutine (16-sector format)*  ______ _____ _____ _____ _____ _____ _____ ______ _____ _____ _____* |      |     |     |     |     |     |     |      |     |     |     |* | GAP1 | $D5 | $AA | $96 | VOL | TRK | SEC | CSUM | $DE | $AA | $EB |* |______|_____|_____|_____|_____|_____|_____|______|_____|_____|_____|** GAP1:         12 to 85 bytes of self sync nibbles ($FF)* VOL:          Volume number (two bytes - 4 & 4 encoded)* TRK:          Track number  (two bytes - 4 & 4 encoded)* SEC:          Sector number (two bytes - 4 & 4 encoded)* CSUM:         Check sum = EOR of volume, track & sector (1 byte)** Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode (q6l, q7l)*               Speed is unknown.** Exit: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = $AA*               X Reg = Unchanged*               Y Reg = $00*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error** csstv holds chksum, sector, track, and volume read.* Uses temps count, last, csum, and 4 bytes at csstv.**    ---- expects ----** Original 10-sector normal density nibls (4-bit), odd bits, then even.**    ---- caution ----** Observe 'no page cross' warnings on some branches!!******************************************************************rdadr16		PROC	align 256		entry	rdadr16E		entry	rdasyn		entry	rda1		entry	rdasn1		entry	rda2		entry	rda3		entry	rdafld		entry	rda4		entry	rda5		entry	rda6		entry	rda7		entry	rderr		longa	off		longi	off				lda	<irqmask		pha		plp			; allow any pending interrupts		sei			; close interrupt windowrdadr16E	lda	#0		sta	>cyareg		; put machine in slow mode		ldy	#$FC		sty	|count		; 'must find' count.rdasyn		iny		bne	rda1		; low order of count.		inc	|count		; (2k nibls to find		bne	rda1		; if more to check			jmp	rderr		; error - couldn't find address mark		rda1		lda	|q6l,x		; read nibl.		bpl	rda1		; *** no page cross! ***rdasn1		cmp	#$D5		; adr mark 1?		bne	rdasyn		; (loop if not)		nop			; added nibl delay.rda2		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	rda2		; *** no page cross! ***		cmp	#$AA		; adr mark 2?		bne	rdasn1		;  (if not, is it am1?)		ldy	#$3		; index for 4-byte read.**            (added nibl delay)*rda3		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	rda3		; *** no page cross! ***		cmp	#$96		; adr mark 3?		bne	rdasn1		;  (if not, is it am1?)			lda	#$0		; init checksum.rdafld		sta	|csumrda4		lda	|q6l,x		; read 'odd bit' nibl.		bpl	rda4		; *** no page cross! ***		rol	a		; align odd bits, '1' into lsb.		sta	|last		;  (save them)rda5		lda	|q6l,x		; read 'even bit' nibl.		bpl	rda5		; *** no page cross! ***		and	|last		; merge odd and even bits.		sta	|csstv,y	; store data byte.		eor	|csum		dey		bpl	rdafld		; loop on 4 data bytes.		tay			; if final checksum		bne	rderr		; nonzero, then error.rda6		lda	|q6l,x		; first bit-slip nibl.		bpl	rda6		; *** no page cross! ***		cmp	#$DE		bne	rderr		; error if nonmatch.		nop			; delayrda7		lda	|q6l,x		; second bit-slip nibl.		bpl	rda7		; *** no page cross! ***		cmp	#$AA		bne	rderr		; error if nonmatch.rddebug		clc			; clear carry on		rts			;  normal read exits.		rderr		sec		rts;	the next few routines are placed in this proc because otherwise it is wasted space.;;	cbl - compute buffer location.;;	entry	(access_flag) != 1 if ProDOS access.;		(interleave_256..) = logical to physical conversion table for DOS.;		(interleave_512..) = logical to physical conversion table for ProDOS.;		(sc_found) = sector read.;		(t.scmap..) = map of sectors already processed.;		(lowsc) = lowest sector to process.;		(highsc) = highest sector to process.;;	exit	(c) set if don't need next sector.;		if need the next sector then [ibufp] = where to store the next sector.;;		alternate entrypoint cblE:;;		(x) = sector to check.		entry	cbl,cblE		cbl		ldx	sect		;sector found on the disk		cblE		lda	>Tscmap,x		bne	cbl4		;if we already processed this disk sector			lda	>access_flag	;access type		dea		bne	cbl1		;if ProDOS access		lda	>interleave_256,x		bra	cbl2cbl1		lda	>interleave_512,xcbl2		cmp	>lowsc		bcc	cbl4		;if not in range		cmp	>highsc				bcc	cbl3		;if less than		bne	cbl4		;if greater than	cbl3		sec		sbc	>lowsc		longmx		and	#$ff		clc		adc	>tk_base		sta	ibbufp+1	;adjust bufptr		skip1				cbl4		sec			;flag that sector can be ignored		shortmx			;reset to short mode		rts;;		mts - mark this sector.;;		entry	(sect) = physical sector that was processed.;			(Tscmap..) = map of processed sectors.;;		exit	(nsec) = (nsec) -1.;			(Tscmap+sect) = $ff.;			z flag will be set if no more sectors to process on this track.		entry	mtsmts		lda	#$ff		ldx	sect		sta	>Tscmap,x	;mark this sector as being processed		lda	>nsec		dea		sta	>nsec		rts;;		pdf - prenibblize data buffer;		entry	pdf* 		If this is a write operation then transfer sector data to* 		bank $00 buffer in preperation for nibblization.*pdf		rep	#$30		longmx		pei	<ibbufp+2	; source buffer		pei	<ibbufp		pea	sys_buffer>>16	; destination buffer		pea	sys_buffer		pea	$0000		; block size		pea	$0100		pea	move_sinc_dinc	; src incr & dest incr		jsl	move_info		jsr	prenib16	;prenibblize the data		shortmx		rts		;	this just fits here...		entry	Tscmap		Tscmap		ds.b	16		; map of used sectors		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* Read subroutine (16-sector format)** Reads encoded bytes into nbuf1 and nbuf2.  First reads nbuf2* high to low, then reads nbuf1 low to high.*  ______ _____ _____ _____ _________________ ______ _____ _____ _____* |      |     |     |     |                 |      |     |     |     |* | GAP2 | $D5 | $AA | $AD | 342 BYTES DATA  | CSUM | $DE | $AA | $EB |* |______|_____|_____|_____|_________________|______|_____|_____|_____|** GAP2:         5 to 10 bytes of self sync nibbles ($FF)* CSUM:         Checksum is 4 & 4 encoded (two bytes)** Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode** Exit: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = $AA*               X Reg = Unchanged*               Y Reg = $00*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error** ---- caution -----** Observe 'no page cross' warnings on some branches!!******************************************************************read16		PROC	align 256		entry	rsync		entry	rd1		entry	rsync1		entry	rd2		entry	rd3		entry	rdata1		entry	rd4		entry	rderr2		entry	ref1		entry	rd5		entry	rd6		entry	ref2		entry	rd7		entry	rdata2		entry	ref3		entry	rd8		entry	rd9		entry	rderr1		entry	rdok		longa	off		longi	off		phb		phk		plb		lda	#$80		sta	>cyareg		; make sure fast mode 				txa			; get slot #.		ora	#$8c		; prepare mods to read routine.		sta	|rd4+1		; warning: the read routine is self modified!!!		sta	|rd5+1		sta	|rd6+1		sta	|rd7+1		sta	|rd8+1				longm		lda	<ibbufp		; modify storage addresses also.		sta	l1		ldy	<ibbufp+2		sty	l1+2				sec		sbc	#$54		sta	l2		bcs	rdf1		dey		secrdf1		sty	l2+2		sbc	#$57		sta	l3		bcs	rdf2		deyrdf2		sty	l3+2		shortm				plb			; restore original data bank		lda	#$0		sta	>cyareg		; go into slow mode				ldy	#$20		; 'must find count'rsync		dey		beq	rderr2		; branch if can't find data header marks.rd1		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	rd1rsync1		eor	#$D5		; first data mark.		bne	rsync		nop			; waste a little time...rd2		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	rd2		cmp	#$AA		; data mark 2		bne	rsync1		; if not, check for first again.		noprd3		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	rd3		cmp	#$AD		; data mark 3		bne	rsync1		; if not, check for data mark 1 again.		ldy	#$AA		lda	#0rdata1		sta	<wtemp		; use zpage for checksum keeping.rd4		ldx	|q6l+$60	; warning: self modified.		bpl	rd4		lda	|dnibl,x		sta	|nbuf2-$aa,y	; save the two-bit groups in nbuf.		eor	<wtemp		; update checksum.		iny			; bump to next nbuf position.		bne	rdata1		; loop for all $56 two-bit groups.		ldy	#$AA		; now read directly into user buffer.		bra	rd5		rderr2		sec				rtsref1					              		sta	[l3],y		rd5		ldx	|q6l+$60		bpl	rd5		eor	|dnibl,x	; get actual 6-bit data from dnib table.		ldx	|nbuf2-$aa,y	; get associated two-bit pattern.		eor	|dnibl2,x	; and combine to form whole byte.		iny		bne	ref1		; loop for $56 bytes.		pha			; save this byte for now, no time to store...		and	#$FC		; strip low bits...		ldy	#$AA		; prepare for next $56 bytes.rd6		ldx	|q6l+$60		bpl	rd6		eor	|dnibl,x		ldx	|nbuf2-$aa,y		eor	|dnibl3,xref2		sta	[l2],y				iny		bne	rd6		; loop until this group of $56 read in.		rd7		ldx	|q6l+$60		bpl	rd7		and	#$FC		ldy	#$AC		; last group is $54 long.rdata2		eor	|dnibl,x		ldx	|nbuf2-$ac,y		eor	|dnibl4,x	; combine to form full byte.ref3		sta	[l1],y		rd8		ldx	|q6l+$60	; warning: self modified.		bpl	rd8		iny		bne	rdata2		and	#$FC		eor	|dnibl,x	; check sum ok?				bne	rderr1		; branch if not.		ldx	<ibslot		; test end marks.		rd9		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	rd9		cmp	#$DE		clc		beq	rdok		; branch if good trailer...rderr1		secrdok		pla			; place last byte into user buffer.		ldy	#$55		sta	[l1],y		;place last byte in buffer		rts		** this subroutine sets the slot dependent track* location.*		entry	settrksettrk		jsr	drvindx		; get index to drive number.		sta	|drv0trk,x		rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* Write subroutine ( 16 sector format)** Writes data from nbuf1 and buf.  First nbuf2 high to low.* Then direct from (buf) low to high.  Self modified code!!!** Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*               Speed = 1 mhz** Exit: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Unchanged*               Y Reg = $00*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error******************************************************************write16		PROC	align 256		entry	wr16		entry	wsync		entry	wdata0		entry	wdata1		entry	wrefd1		entry	wdata2		entry	wrefa1		entry	wrefd2		entry	wrefa2		entry	wdata3		entry	wrefa3		entry	wrefd3		entry	wrefa4		entry	wrefa5		entry	wrtodd		entry	wrefd4		entry	wrefa6		entry	wdne1		entry	wdata4		entry	wdone		entry	wrefd5		entry	wrtendmk		entry	wexit					;using driver_data		longa	off		longi	off		sec			; anticipate wprot err.		lda	|q6h,x		lda	|q7l,x		; sense wprot flag.		bpl	@wr16		jmp	wexit		; exit if write protected@wr16		lda	#$0		sta	>cyareg		; reset to slow modewr16		lda	|nbuf2		sta	<wtemp		lda	#$FF		; sync data.		sta	|q7h,x		; (5) goto write mode		ora	|q6l,x		; (4)		ldy	#$4		; (2) for five nibls.		nop			; (2)		pha			; (3)		pla			; (4)wsync		pha			; (3) exact timing.		pla			; (4) exact timing.		jsr	wnibl7		; (13,9,6)  write sync.		dey			; (2)		bne	wsync		; (3-)  must not cross page!		lda	#$D5		; (2)  1st data mark.		jsr	wnibl9		; (15,9,6)		lda	#$AA		; (2)  2nd data mark.		jsr	wnibl9		; (15,9,6)		lda	#$AD		; (2)  3rd data mark.		jsr	wnibl9		; (15,9,6)		tya			; (2) zero checksum 		ldy	#$56		; (2) nbuf2 index		bne	wdata1		; (3)branch always taken. wdata0		lda	|nbuf2,y	; (4) prior 6-bit nibl.wdata1		eor	|nbuf2-1,y	; (5) xor with current.		tax			; (2) index to 7-bit nibl (nbuf2 must be on page boundary).		lda	|nibl,x		; (4) must not cross page boundary 		ldx	<ibslot		; (3) restore slot index. 		sta	|q6h,x		; (5) store encoded byte.		lda	|q6l,x		; (4) time must = 32 us per byte!		dey			; (2)		bne	wdata0		; (3-) must not cross page boundary 		lda	<wtemp		; (3) get prior nibl (from nbuf2).wrefd1		ldy	#0		; (2) warning: load value modified by prenib!wdata2wrefa1		eor	|$1000,y	; (4) warning: address modified by prenib!		and	#$FC		; (2)		tax			; (2) index to nibl table		lda	|nibl,x		; (4)wrefd2		ldx	#$60		; (2) warning: load value modified by prenib		sta	|q6h,x		; (5) write nibl.		lda	|q6l,x		; (4) handshake.wrefa2		lda	|$1000,y	; (4) prior nibl. warning: address modified by prenib.		iny			; (2) all done with this page?		bne	wdata2		; (3-) loop until page end.		lda	<midnib1	; (3) get next (precalculated and translated) nibl.		beq	wdone		; (2+) branch if code writen was page aligned.		lda	<yend		; (3) get byte address of last byte to be written.		beq	wdata4		; (2+) branch if only 1 byte left to write.		lsr	a		; (2) test for odd or even last byte (carry set or clear)		lda	<midnib1	; (3) restore nibl to acc.		sta	|q6h,x		; (5)		lda	|q6l,x		; (4)		lda	<midnib2	; (3) =byte 0 of second page. xor'd with byte 1 if above test set carry.		nop			; (2) waste time.		iny			; (2) y=1		bcs	wrtodd		; (2+) branch if last byte to be odd.wdata3wrefa3		eor	|$1100,y	; (4) warning: address modified by prenib.		and	#$FC		; (2) strip low 2 bits.		tax			; (2) index to nibl table.		lda	|nibl,x		; (4) get nibl.wrefd3		ldx	#$60		; (2) restore slot index. warning: modified by prenib.		sta	|q6h,x		; (5)		lda	|q6l,x		; (4)wrefa4		lda	|$1100,y	; (4) warning: modified by prenib.		iny			; (2) got prior nibl, bump to next.wrefa5		eor	|$1100,y	; (4) warning: modified by prenib.wrtodd		cpy	<yend		; (3) set carry if this is last nibl.		and	#$FC		; (2)		tax			; (2) 		lda	|nibl,x		; (4)wrefd4		ldx	#$60		; (2) restore slot. warning: modified by prenib.		sta	|q6h,x		; (5) 		lda	|q6l,x		; (4) wrefa6		lda	|$1100,y	; (4) get prior. warning: these warnings are all the same.		iny			; (2) 		bcc	wdata3		; (3-) branch if that was not the last.		bcs	wdne1		; (3) waste 3 cycles, branch alwayswdne1		bcs	wdone		; (3) branch alwayswdata4		lda	|midnib1	; (4) absolute reference to zero page.		sta	|q6h,x		; (5)		lda	|q6l,x		; (4)		pha			; (3) waste 14 us total.		pla			; (4)		pha			; (3)		pla			; (4) wdone		ldx	<lstnib		; (3) last nibl (and w/$fc) for checksum.		lda	|nibl,x		; (4)wrefd5		ldx	#$60		; (2) restore slot. warning: see above warnings...		sta	|q6h,x		; (5) 		lda	|q6l,x		; (4)		ldy	#0		; (2) set y to index end mark table. 		pha			; (3) waste another 11 us. 		pla			; (4) 		nop			; (2) 		nop			; (2) wrtendmk		lda	|endmrks,y	; (4) dm4, dm5, dm6, and turn off byte.		jsr	wnibl		; (15,6)    write it.		iny			; (2)		cpy	#4		; (2) have all end marks been written? 		bne	wrtendmk	; (3)		clc			; (2,9) wexit		lda	|q7l,x		; out of write mode.		lda	|q6l,x		; to read mode.		lda	#$80		sta	>cyareg		rts			; return from write.		eject*******************************************************************   7-bit nibl write subrs**   a-reg or'd prior exit*       carry cleared******************************************************************		entry	wnibl9		entry	wnibl7		entry	wniblwnibl9		clc			; (2)  9 cycles, then write.wnibl7		pha			; (3)  7 cycles, then write.		pla			; (4)wnibl		sta	|q6h,x		; (5)  nibl write sub.		ora	|q6l,x		; (4)  clobbers acc, not carry.		rts			; (6) 		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* Preniblize subroutine (16 sector format)** Converts 256 bytes of user data in (buf) into 6 bit nibls* into nbuf2. High 6 bits are translated directly by the write* routines.** Entry: via a 'JSR'*                 Buf = Word pointer to 256 bytes of user data*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode** Exit: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error** Write routine modified to do direct conversion of high* 6 bits of users buffer data.******************************************************************prenib16	PROC		entry	prenib1		entry	prenib2		entry	prenib3		entry	prenib4		entry	prn1		entry	prn2		entry	prn3		entry	wmod1		entry	wmod2		entry	wmod3					;using   driver_data		phb			; need our bank for self modification		phk		plb		longa	on		longi	on		lda	#sys_buffer		sta	l1		sep	#$30		longa	off		longi	off				lda	<l1		; first self modify addresses so we can be fast!		ldy	<l1+1		; y contains high order address. 		clc			; all offsets are -$aa... 		adc	#2		; the highest set is buf+$ac 		bcc	prenib1		; branch if no carry. 		iny			; otherwise add carry to high address. prenib1		sta	|prn3+1		; self mod 3		sty	|prn3+2				sec			sbc	#$56		; middle set is buf+$56 		bcs	prenib2		; branch if no borrow 		dey			; otherwise deduct from high..prenib2		sta	|prn2+1		; self mod 2.		sty	|prn2+2				sec		sbc	#$56		; low set is exactly buf.		bcs	prenib3		deyprenib3		sta	|prn1+1		; self mod 1.		sty	|prn1+2		plb			; back to I/O bank		ldy	#$AA		; count up to 0. prenib4prn1		lda	|$1000,y	; fetch byte from lowest group. warning: self modified.		and	#$3		; strip high 6 bits. 		tax			; index to 2 bit equiv.		lda	|twobit1,x			pha			; save pattern prn2		lda	|$1056,y	; fetch from middle group		and	#3				tax			pla			; restore pattern.		ora	twobit2,x	; combine second group with first. 		pha			; save new pattern. prn3		lda	|$10ac,y	; get highest group.		and	#3				tax			pla			; restore new pattern. 		ora	|twobit3,x	; and form final nibl. 		pha		tya		eor	#$FF		tax		pla		sta	|nbuf2,x	; save in nibl buffer! 		iny			; bump to next set. 		bne	prenib4		; loop until all $56 nibls formed. 		ldy	<l1		; now prepare data bytes for write16 routine.		dey			; prepare end addr.		sty	<yend		lda	<l1		sta	>wrefd1+1	; warning: the following storage addresses starting		beq	wmod1		;  with 'wref' are referces into code space,		eor	#$FF		;  changed by this routine.		tay			; index to last byte of page pointed to by buf.		lda	(<l1),y		; pre-niblize the last byte of the page with		iny			;  the first byte of the next page.		eor	(<l1),y		and	#$FC		tax		lda	|nibl,x		; get disk 7-bit nibl equivalent.wmod1		sta	<midnib1		beq	wmod3		; branch if data to be written is page aligned.		lda	<yend		; find out if last byte is even or odd address.		lsr	a		; shift even/oddness into carry		lda	(<l1),y		; if even, then leave in tact.		bcc	wmod2		; branch if odd.		iny			; if even, then pre-xor with byte 1.		eor	(<l1),ywmod2		sta	<midnib2	; save result for write routine.wmod3		ldy	#$FF		; index to last byte of data to be writen		lda	(<l1),y		;  to be used as checksum.		and	#$FC		; strip extra bits		phb			; need our bank for self modification		phk		plb		sta	<lstnib		; save it.		ldy	<l1+1		; now modify address reference to user data.		sty	|wrefa1+2		sty	|wrefa2+2		iny		sty	|wrefa3+2		sty	|wrefa4+2		sty	|wrefa5+2		sty	|wrefa6+2		ldx	<ibslot		; and lastly index references to controller.		stx	|wrefd2+1			stx	|wrefd3+1			stx	|wrefd4+1			stx	|wrefd5+1			plb		rts			; all done.		eject******************************************************************* Checks to see if this access is to the same device as the* previous access.** Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*               Speed = 1 mhz** Exit: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error******************************************************************		entry	chkprev		entry	chkpv1		entry	chkpv2chkprev		longa	off		longi	off		lda	<ibslot		; same slot as last previous access		cmp	<iobpsn		bne	not_same		lda	<ibdrvn		; same unit as last previous access		cmp	<iobpdn		beq	chkpv2not_same		lda	#01		sta	|montimehchkpv1		ldx	<ibslot		beq	chkpv2		; branch if no previous ever (boot only)		jsr	chkdrv0		; find out if previous drive running. 		beq	chkpv2		; branch if stopped.		lda	#1		; waste some time.		jsr	mswait		lda	|montimeh		bne	chkpv1chkpv2		rts		eject******************************************************************* Reset all phase lines to the drive in preperation for I/O.** Entry: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*               Speed = 1 mhz** ExIt: via a 'rts'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Current program bank*             Dir Reg = Absolute zero page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1******************************************************************		entry	rsetphsersetphse		longa	off		longi	off		ldx	<ibslot		; get unit number		lda	|phaseoff+0,x	; make sure all motor phases		lda	|phaseoff+2,x	; are off		lda	|phaseoff+4,x		lda	|phaseoff+6,x		rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* DRIVER SUBROUTINE: Format_media** Disk][ sector looks like:*  _____ ______ _____ ______ ______________ _______ ______ _____* |     |      |     |      |              |       |      |     |* | GAP | ADDR | GAP | DATA |  342 BYTES   | CHECK | END  | GAP |* |  1  | MARK |  2  | MARK |  DATA FIELD  |  SUM  | MARK |  3  |* |_____|______|_____|______|______________|_______|______|_____|** GAP 1:        12 to 85 bytes of self sync nibbles ($FF)* ADDR MARK:    $D5, $AA, $96, volume, track, sector & checksum* GAP 2:        5 to 10 bytes of self sync nibbles ($FF)* DATA MARK:    $D5, $AA, $AD* DATA FIELD:   342 bytes of six and two encoded data* CHECKSUM:     1 byte eor checksum* END MARK:     $DE, $AA, $EB, $FF* GAP 3:        16 to 28 bytes of self sync nibbles ($FF)** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed = 1 mHz*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*              <slotz = Slot * 16** EXIT: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error******************************************************************format_media	PROC						;using   driver_data		longa	off		longi	off		lda	#$D7		; almost 1 second		sta	|montimeh** Recalibrate the read/write head.*		jsr	drvindx		; get current track index this drive		lda	#80		; pretend on track 80		sta	>drv0trk,x		lda	#0		; destination track is zero		jsr	myseek		; move the headwait_up		lda	|montimeh	; motor up to speed?		beq	up_to_speed	; yes		jsr	mswait		; else continue delay		bra	wait_up** Initialize things.*up_to_speed 		lda	<ibvol		; wildcard volume #?		bne	@1		; no...		lda	#254		; else default it (like DOS 3.3)		sta	<ibvol@1		lda	#$AA		; time dependent references		sta	<aa		lda	#$1D		; number of selfsync nibbles		sta	<nsync		lda	#0		; start on track zero		sta	<ibtrkformat_track		lda	<ibtrk		; seek to track to be formatted		ldx	<ibslot		jsr	myseek		ldx	<ibslot		; get slot * 16		lda	|q6h,x		; to sense mode (check WRPROT)		lda	|q7l,x		tay		lda	|q7l,x		; back into read mode		lda	|q6l,x		tya		bpl	write_enable	; if write enabled		lda	#drvr_wr_prot	; else return write protected error		bra	format_donewrite_enable		jsr	write_fmt_16	; write & verify track		bcc	trk_fmt_ok	; if this track formatted okreturn_io_err		lda	#drvr_io_error	; else return an I/O error		bra	format_done** Track formatted ok.  Check if drive speed is within exceptable limits.*trk_fmt_ok		ldy	<nsync		; gaps to small?		cpy	#$0E		blt	return_io_err	; yes		cpy	#$1B		; gaps to large?		bge	return_io_err	; yes** Drive speed appears to be within limits.  Open an interrupt* window just in case an IRQ is pending.*track_ok		lda	<irqmask		pha		plp		sei			; close interrupt window		lda	#$10		; to find sector zero		sta	|retrycntfind_sec_0		dec	|retrycnt	; any more retries		bmi	return_io_err	; no		ldx	<ibslot		; need slot * 16		jsr	rdadr16E	; find address field  DEBUG		bcs	find_sec_0	; retry if cant find address field		lda	|sect		; check sector that was read		bne	find_sec_0	; if not sector zero		ldx	<ibslot		; need slot * 16		jsr	verify16	; now read data field		bcs	find_sec_0	; if cant read data field then retry** Head is now properly positioned for optimum latency on seek to next track.*		inc	<ibtrk		lda	<ibtrk		cmp	#35		blt	format_track		lda	#no_errorformat_done		pha		ldx	<ibslot		; need slot * 16		lda	|motoroff,x	; turn motor off		lda	#0		; restore r/w head to track zero		jsr	myseek		pla		sta	<ibstat		rts		eject******************************************************************* VERIFY16** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed = 1 mHz*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*              <slotz = Slot * 16** EXIT: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error******************************************************************		entry	verify16verify16		longa	off		longi	off		lda	#$00		; ensure 1Mhz clock		sta	>cyareg		ldy	#$20		; 'must find' countvsync		dey		beq	verr		; if cant find marks then errorv1		lda	|q6l,x		; read nibl		bpl	v1		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***vsync1		eor	#$D5		; data mark #1?		bne	vsync		; no		nopv2		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	v2		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		cmp	#$AA		; data mark #2?		bne	vsync1		; no, is it data mark #1?		ldy	#$56		; init nbuf2 indexv3		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	v3		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		cmp	#$AD		; data mark #3		bne	vsync1		; no, is it data mark #1?		lda	#$00		; init checksumvdata1		dey		sty	<idxv4		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	v4		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		cmp	#$96		; is it one of our zeros?		bne	verr		; no, exit with an error		ldy	<idx		bne	vdata1vdata2		sty	<idxv5		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	v5		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		cmp	#$96		; is it one of our zeros?		bne	verr		; no, exit with an error		ldy	<idx		iny		bne	vdata2v6		lda	|q6l,x		; read 7 bit checksum nibl		bpl	v6		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		cmp	#$96		; checksum correct?		bne	verr		; no, exit with an errorv7		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	v7		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		cmp	#$DE		; first bit slip mark?		bne	verr		; no, exit with an errorv8		lda	|q6l,x		bpl	v8		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		cmp	#$AA		; second bit slip mark?		bne	verr		; no, exit with an error		clc		dc.b	$B0		; BCS opcode (skip SEC)verr		sec		lda	#$80		; reset to fast clock		sta	>cyareg		rts		ENDP		EJECT******************************************************************* FORMAT16** This routine writes a sector of 256 $00's (342 $96's).* Code is very time critical.  Observe all page cross warnings.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed = 1 mHz*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*              <slotz = Slot * 16** EXIT: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1******************************************************************format16	PROC	align		256		longa	off		longi	off		lda	#$00		; slow mode		sta	>cyareg		jsr	fmt_exit	; delay		bit	|q6h,x		; switch to write sense/setup mode		lda	#$FF		; self sync data		sta	|q7h,x		; write 1st nibl		cmp	|q6l,x		pha		pla		nop		ldy	#4		; for 5 niblsfsync		pha		pla		jsr	fnibl7		; write sync		dey		bne	fsync		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		lda	#$D5		; write 1st address mark		jsr	fnibl9		lda	#$AA		; write 2nd address mark		jsr	fnibl9		lda	#$AD		; write 3rd address mark		jsr	fnibl9		ldy	#$56		; 1st loop: write 86 zeros		nop		nop		nop		bne	fdata1		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***fdata0		jsr	fmt_exitfdata1		nop		nop		lda	#$96		; write zeros into data field		sta	|q6h,x		cmp	|q6l,x		dey		bne	fdata0		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		bit	<$00		; then write additional 256 zeros		nopfdata2		jsr	fmt_exit		lda	#$96		; write zeros into data field		sta	|q6h,x		cmp	|q6l,x		lda	#$96		; load for checksum fall through		nop		iny		bne	fdata2		; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		jsr	fnibl9		; write checksum		lda	#$DE		; write 1st bit slip mark		jsr	fnibl9		lda	#$AA		; write 2nd bit slip mark		jsr	fnibl9		lda	#$EB		; write 3rd bit slip mark		jsr	fnibl9		lda	#$FF		; turn off byte		jsr	fnibl9		lda	|q7l,x		; switch back to read mode		lda	|q6l,x		lda	#$80		; fast mode		sta	>cyaregfmt_exit		rtsfnibl9		nop			; 9 cycles, then writefnibl7		pha			; 7 cycles, then write		pla		sta	|q6h,x		cmp	|q6l,x		rts		eject******************************************************************* WRITE ADDRESS 16** Writes specified number fo 40 uS (10 bit) self sync nibls,* address marks and fields.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Number of self sync nibbles*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed = 1 mHz*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*              <slotz = Slot * 16** EXIT: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error******************************************************************		entry	wr_adr_16wr_adr_16		longa	off		longi	off		lda	#0		; slow mode		sta	>cyareg		sei			; no interrupts for now* we added these to lines to fix formating to disk2 card problem		lda	|q6h,x		;into write setup mode		lda	|q7l,x* end of our patch		lda	#$FF		; self sync nibble		sta	|q7h,x		cmp	|q6l,x		pha		plawr_sync1		jsr	wr_adr_rts1	; for 40uS nibbles		jsr	wr_adr_rts1		sta	|q6h,x		; write nibble		cmp	|q6l,x		nop		dey		bne	wr_sync1	; *** NO PAGE CROSS ***		lda	#$D5		; write 1st address mark		jsr	wniblb2		lda	#$AA		; write 2nd address mark		jsr	wniblb2		lda	#$96		; write 3rd address mark		jsr	wniblb2		lda	<ibvol		; write volume		jsr	wbyte		lda	<ibtrk		; write track		jsr	wbyte		lda	<ibsect		; write sector		jsr	wbyte		lda	<ibvol		; form address field checksum		eor	<ibtrk		eor	<ibsect		pha			; save for even bits		lsr	a		ora	<aa		; set clock bits** Precise timing, 32 cycles per nibblized byte)*		sta	|q6h,x		; write checksum odd bits		lda	|q6l,x		pla		ora	#$AA		; set clock bits		jsr	wnibla		lda	#$DE		; end mark 1		jsr	wniblb2		lda	#$AA		; end mark 2		jsr	wniblb2		lda	#$EB		; end mark 3		jsr	wniblb2		clc			; indicate no wrprot errorwr_adr_rts		lda	|q7l,x		; out of write mode		lda	|q6l,x		lda	#$80		; fast mode		sta	 >cyaregwr_adr_rts1		rtswbyte		pha			; preserve for even bits		lsr	a		; align odd bits		ora	<aa		; set clock bits		sta	|q6h,x		; write nibble		cmp	|q6l,x		pla			; recover even bits		nop		nop		nop		ora	#$AA		; set clock bitswnibla		nopwniblb2		nop		pha		pla		sta	|q6h,x		cmp	|q6l,x		rts		eject******************************************************************* WRITE_FORMAT_16** We have a counter (trkretry) which prevents wtrack16 from* retrying forever.  The extensive retries caused the track* to precess on successive writes, possibly allowing a damaged* spot on the media to be slit into an intersector gap.* Subsequent data writes could then encounter the damaged area.* Finally, the routine verifies that the first sector encountered* is sector 0, and that all 16 sectors are readable withing* 2 revolutions of the disk.  If the first sector is not zero* then the current number of self sync nibls is decremented by 1.* Then sector 15 is located so as to position the track for a* rewrite.  If unable to read any sector then the entire track* will be rewritten.** ENTRY: via a 'JSR'*               A Reg = Undefined*               X Reg = Slot * 16*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x x  1*               Speed = 1 mHz*            IWM Mode = Read Mode*              <slotz = Slot * 16** EXIT: via a 'RTS'*               A Reg = Error code*               X Reg = Undefined*               Y Reg = Undefined*               B Reg = Bank $00*             Dir Reg = Absolute Zero Page*               P Reg = N V M X D I Z C  E*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 0  1  if no error*                       x x 1 1 0 1 x 1  1  if error******************************************************************		entry	write_fmt_16write_fmt_16		longa	off		longi	off		lda	#3		; max retries per track		sta	<trkretry** On first attempt, deliberately write to large a seam.* This ensures that all of the track is erased.*wr_retry		ldy	#128		; 128 nibls prior to sector zero		lda	#0		sta	<ibsect		bra	wr_sect_0wr_sect		ldy	<nsync		; current number of gap selfsync niblswr_sect_0		ldx	<ibslot		jsr	wr_adr_16	; write gap and adr field		ldx	<ibslot		jsr	format16	; write sector from nbuf1, nbuf2		inc	<ibsect		lda	<ibsect		cmp	#16		bcc	wr_sect		; do all 16 sectors				eject** Start of track verify routine.*		ldy	#16-1		; sector zero is special		sty	<ibsect		lda	#16		sta	|retrycnt		clr_found	sta	|found,y	; mark each sector as not found		dey		bpl	clr_found** Delay for 40 mS per nsysc byte to ensure that the* gap between sector 15 and 0 is large enough.*		lda	#0		sta	>cyareg		; make sure slow mode				lda	<nsync		; get current count		sec		sbc	#5		; 2 already past & 5 for self sync		taysec_0_delay		jsr	wexit		jsr	wexit		pha		pla		nop		nop		dey		bne	sec_0_delay		lda	#$80		; back to fast clock		sta	>cyareg** See if we have a sector zero here*		ldx	<ibslot		; need slot * 16		jsr	rdadr16E	; read next address field.DEBUG		bcs	rewrite		; err, locate sect 15 & rewrite track		lda	|sect		; was it sector zero?		beq	verify_data	; yes, now verify data field** Not sector zero.  Gaps are to large.  Rewrite to reduce gap size.*		dec	<nsync		lda	<nsync		cmp	#$0E		; are gaps already to small?		bge	rewrite		; no, go ahead and rewrite track		lda	#drvr_io_error		sec		rts** Make sure we can read the track we just wrote.*verify_sector		ldx	<ibslot		; need slot * 16		jsr	rdadr16E	; read address field		bcs	verify_err	; retry if cant read address fieldverify_data			ldx	<ibslot		; need slot * 16		jsr	verify16	; verify data field		bcs	verify_err	; retry if cant read data		ldy	|sect		; this is the sector we just read		lda	|found,y	; already found?		bmi	verify_err	; yes, ignore it		lda	#$FF		; else mark it as found		sta	|found,y		dec	<ibsect		; next sector to find		bpl	verify_sector	; loop for all 16 sectors		lda	#no_error		clc		rts** Either could not read address marks, data or sector was previously* verified.  In any case, if retry count is not exhausted then try* to verify the sector again.*verify_err		dec	|retrycnt	; next of 48 sector retries		bne	verify_sector		dec	|trkretry	; should track be rewritten?		bne	rewrite		; yes		lda	#drvr_io_error		sec		rts** Could not verify the track.  Find sector 15 before rewritting.*rewrite		lda	<ibtrk		; if not track zero then dont open		bne	no_window	; an interrupt window		lda	<irqmask		pha		plp		seino_window		lda	#$20		; maximum retries = 2 revolutions		sta	|retrycntfind_sec_15		ldx	<ibslot		; need slot * 16		jsr	rdadr16E	; read address field		bcs	not_sec_15	; if cant read		lda	<ibsect		; sector that was read		cmp	#15		; was it sector 15?		beq	found_sec_15	; yesnot_sec_15		dec	|retrycnt		bne	find_sec_15		secwexit		rts** Delay to let most of sector 15's data pass by, then go back and* rewrite the track (including the 28 nibblies of seam).  This assures* that we will rewrite the track entirely, and that sector zero will be* aligned at roughly the same place as it was on the prior try.*found_sec_15		lda	#$00		; slow clock		sta	>cyareg		ldx	#342-128	; let most go byverify_delay		jsr	wexit		jsr	wexit		bit	<$00		dex		bne	verify_delay		lda	#$80		; fast clock		sta	>cyareg		jmp	wr_retry		entry	highsc,lowsc,nsec,nsec2,secleft,tk_base		entry	seccnt		entry	nxtwrt				highsc		ds.b	2lowsc		ds.b	2	nsec		ds.b	2nsec2		ds.b	2secleft		ds.b	2tk_base		ds.b	2nxtwrt		ds.b	2seccnt		dc.w	0		ENDP		END